# Client Intake Form

**Company:** Northwind Logistics
**Industry:** Mid-market freight brokerage
**Size:** ~200 employees, 40 dispatchers, ~600 contracted drivers
**Headquarters:** Columbus, OH
**Annual revenue:** ~$85M (2025)

## Primary Contact
- **Name:** Sarah Chen
- **Title:** VP Operations
- **Email:** sarah.chen@northwindlog.com
- **Role:** Champion. Owns the operational pain. Has CFO buy-in to fund a Phase 1 engagement.

## Other Stakeholders
- **Marcus Patel** — CTO. Required for technical sign-off. Owns the dispatch tool (custom Rails app, ~7 years old). Has been pushing internally for a full rebuild.
- **Rita Donovan** — CFO. Controls the budget. Skeptical of consulting engagements; got burned by a previous vendor in 2023.
- **Rajiv Mehta** — Head of Compliance (mentioned but not yet engaged). Owns ELD compliance.

## Stated Ask (verbatim from intro email)
> "Our dispatcher workflow is killing us. Too much manual entry between our custom dispatch tool and Salesforce, drivers hate the mobile app, and finance is 3 weeks behind on invoicing because the data never lines up. We need help figuring out where to start."

## Budget Signal
- CFO has approved a 6-month Phase 1 engagement.
- No hard number disclosed in writing. (Sarah has hinted at a range in conversation.)
- Strong preference for fixed-fee with milestone payments over T&M.

## Timeline
- Pilot in production by end of Q3 (Sept 30).
- ELD compliance deadline in November (federal mandate update; details unclear, will be discussed on the call).

## Existing Tech Stack
- **Dispatch tool:** Custom Rails 5 app, internally maintained by 2 engineers
- **CRM:** Salesforce (Sales Cloud)
- **TMS (Transportation Management System):** Currently evaluating vendors. No selection made.
- **Driver mobile app:** Custom React Native app, last major update in 2023
- **Accounting:** NetSuite
- **Data warehouse:** None (BI is run out of Excel exports from Salesforce)

## Background Notes
- Northwind grew 40% in 2024 by acquiring two smaller brokerages. Tech integration from those acquisitions is incomplete.
- Sarah has asked us specifically because we did similar work for a peer brokerage (Cascade Freight) in 2024.
- This is a competitive engagement — they are also talking to two other firms.


